 "drivingQuestion": "Is the laborers' interval twice a week (mishna) or once (baraita)?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Contradiction resolved by distinguishing work location, supported by a baraita",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "ketubot.62a.9",
   "daf": "62a",
   "sentenceId": 8,
   "he": "וְהַפּוֹעֲלִים שְׁתַּיִם בַּשַּׁבָּת. וְהָתַנְיָא: הַפּוֹעֲלִים אַחַת בַּשַּׁבָּת! אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹסֵי בְּרַבִּי חֲנִינָא, לָא קַשְׁיָא: כָּאן בְּעוֹשִׂין מְלָאכָה בְּעִירָן, כָּאן בְּעוֹשִׂין מְלָאכָה בְּעִיר אַחֶרֶת. תַּנְיָא נָמֵי הָכִי: הַפּוֹעֲלִים שְׁתַּיִם בַּשַּׁבָּת, בַּמֶּה דְּבָרִים אֲמוּרִים — בְּעוֹשִׂין מְלָאכָה בְּעִירָן, אֲבָל בְּעוֹשִׂין מְלָאכָה בְּעִיר אַחֶרֶת — אַחַת בַּשַּׁבָּת.",
   "en": "§ The mishna said: The set interval for «laborers» to fulfill their conjugal obligations to their wives is «twice a week.» The Gemara asks: «Isn’t it taught» in a baraita: For «laborers, once a week? Rabbi Yosei, son of Rabbi Ḥanina, said:» This is «not difficult: Here,» the case is «where they work in their own city. There,» the case is «where they work in another city. This is also taught» in the Tosefta (5:6): For «laborers, twice a week. In what» case «is this statement said?» It is «when they work in their own city, but when they work in another city,» the set interval for their conjugal obligations is «once a week.»"
  }
 ],
